+# Fix: HR corridors clamped to the watch's own zones
+
+## Change
+`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: the lower bound key is now `start` instead of `value`:
+`{"units": "%lthr", "start": lo, "end": hi}`.
+
+## Why
+`readback/watch-notes.md` shows every corridor displayed as a watch zone band
+(e.g. planned 75–82% = 129–141 bpm, shown 137–151), even though the API
+accepted and returned the event unchanged. `{value, end}` is exported to FIT
+as a Lap-HR / zone target, which the watch clamps to its own zones (LTHR 168).
+`{start, end}` is exported as an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm computed by
+Intervals from its stored LTHR (172). Units stay `%lthr`, so Intervals does the
+conversion (the absolute-bpm attempts gave 214–249 and 101).
+
+## Which parts of the colleague's note I used
+- Used: the `start`/`end` vs `value`/`end` finding, and keeping `%lthr` units
+  (matches our earlier failed bpm attempts in the watch notes).
+- Not used: the top-level `description` text grammar. Our readback has
+  `workout_doc.steps` populated and the problem reported is the watch targets,
+  not the web UI. Adding it would be unverified here and, per the note, a
+  parser stumble erases both representations. Worth doing separately if the
+  web UI shows no step chart.
+- Not used: the reproduction steps (they need the API key, athlete id and a
+  watch sync).
+
+## Not verified
+I could not push or sync a watch (no credentials, nothing external sent). To
+verify: push `gen.py` output, read it back (`steps` must be non-empty), sync,
+and expect Tempo 151–160, Float 129–141 on the watch.
